# Monastery Flock's ruling (2014-09-20): an attacking face-down Monastery Flock turned face up keeps attacking though it now
# has defender - defender only stops it being declared as an attacker (CR 702.3b), and turning face up changes only its
# characteristics, never its combat status (CR 708.8, 506.4a) - and turned up before blockers are declared it has flying, so a
# creature without flying or reach can't block it (CR 702.9b). On turn 3 the face-down 2/2 and Kobolds of Kher Keep attack;
# in the declare attackers step Mox Sapphire pays the {U} to turn it up. Bot2's Memnite may block the Kobolds (which
# die), not the Flock.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Monastery Flock
Mox Sapphire
Kobolds of Kher Keep
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Memnite
Island x23

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Monastery Flock.Cast(Ability: Morph)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Kobolds of Kher Keep.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(#1 > Bot2; Kobolds of Kher Keep > Bot2)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.#1.Activate(Ability: morph cost)
? Combat.Attackers = Kobolds of Kher Keep > Bot2; Monastery Flock > Bot2
? Bot1.Battlefield.Monastery Flock.Keywords = Defender; Flying; Morph
[T3 Bot1.DeclareBlockers]
! Bot2.Block(Memnite > Monastery Flock)
Bot2.Block(Memnite > Kobolds of Kher Keep)
? Combat.Attackers = Kobolds of Kher Keep > Bot2; Monastery Flock > Bot2
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Kobolds of Kher Keep; Black Lotus
Bot1.Battlefield.Monastery Flock.Tapped = true
